{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"negligent-paranoid-raccoon","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\nEpic pompous-vitriolic-macaw moved the configured models to Opus 5.5, Sonnet 5.5 and Haiku 5.5, but 2 hard-coded defaults in `src/rebar` still name the old generation:\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py:448`: `chunk_by_facet(..., model: str = \"claude-sonnet-4-6\", ...)`. The production caller (`pass1.py:285`) passes `cfg.model`, so a call that omits `model` sizes chunks for the wrong model.\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/fixture_emit.py:18`: `_MODEL = \"anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6\"`, which is stamped into emitted eval fixtures.\n\nThe 4.x entries in `capabilities.py` and `model_classes.py` are per-model tables, not defaults, and may stay.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `chunk_by_facet` takes no old-generation default: either `model` is required or it defaults to the configured standard class.\n- [ ] `fixture_emit` stamps a current-generation model or the configured one.\n- [ ] A test fails if a function default or module constant in `src/rebar` names a pre-5.5 Claude id outside the per-model capability tables.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","id":"ac9f-db05-bc10-41a0","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Old-generation model ids in src/rebar defaults"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794547687212760001,"uuid":"461faa8c-5fd6-443b-9243-550c20b5f80b"}